t: let's make this as ASSERT_EQ since the following lines should not be executed if this is not true?"],["27e42b45_31dc6ef1",67,0,1,"why did we need a runloop for this test?"],["50aef57e_f9d5a698",67,0,1,"I think we have this exact set of lines in almost all the new tests? Instead of QueryHistoryDone, can we have a helper QueryHistory which does all this?"]],0,3579],[7245870,20432,22,0.622,0.461,[[19,547]],[],0,3580],[7216548,20433,313,6.536,5.29,[[1,144]],[["1cce5b17_8b2707b9",68,0,0,"nit: Since this is not being used by BrowsingHistoryHandlerTest, let's make this a free function instead?"],["5468f18f_0e3fcb1f",69,0,1,"Can you please add a `CHECK_NE(state->local_status, NO_DEPENDENCY)` here? Because if in some weird case, this is equal, we're querying both sources."],["a7f8802b_543b055c",1,0,1,"Can you please add a comment here that unlike QueryHistoryLocalPagingFull, the local and remote query results return reached_beginning."],["d2f7aa3f_3df917c2",1,0,1,"Is this the desired behavior in this case? Can you please document in which case this can happen? (GU response not received for some reason?)"],["fc46f00e_5959108f",69,0,1,"Are we sure this is sorted? Another place is using `OldestTime()` instead."]],0,3581],[7246716,20437,576,9.596,7.813,[[1,1.0,145,580]],[],0,3582],[7260537,20437,9,0.75,0.55,[[30,0.75,114,7],[19,0.25,548,2]],[],0,3583],[7232242,20440,570,9.596,7.813,[[30,0.911,115,529],[39,0.036,31,18],[11,0.019,92,9],[26,0.017,114,9],[0,0.007,317,2],[74,0.007,5,2],[75,0.003,77,1]],[["144d5e01_6b786f0a",70,-8,1,"We should allow the check for OAuth client here - similar to https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7229106/7/components/signin/public/identity_manager/access_token_restriction.cc#2…"],["92307c3f_242ecc69",71,-8,0,"I suggest we add an https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:components/signin/public/base/oauth_consumer_id.h that is specific to this file. Let's call it sync_device_stats. We can…"],["234f9b17_d1a5ee89",71,-3,1,"Optional: using booleans doesn't help readability here. I think you could introduce an enum instead, and use kFail here (vs kSuccess) or more optionally specific failure codes."],["3ecbfaf7_ba3634c0",72,-3,1,"Would sync_metrics be simple to rename in the future? If not, I would rather use a more specific name, e.g. sync_device_statistics_metrics."],["499f77b6_8854e8de",73,-3,1,"WDYT about moving `callback` to Start()? It reads really odd here IMO. Also: why does it take a DeviceStatisticsRequest* argument? It seems redundant, because `this` already implies a…"],["4abff0bd_a6e32a4c",71,-3,1,"We should remove this IMO, at most instrument UMA metrics to monitor things are WAI."],["6dd2c7ec_590b9d7b",71,-3,1,"Is this accurate?"],["c3563d33_aa8c403f",70,-3,1,"Nit: how about extracting this to a constant, and reference it also from DeviceStatisticsRequest."],["c40ba60c_a6d273ca",73,-3,1,"Nit: disallow copy and move explicitly?"],["e9ae380b_95426f3b",73,-3,1,"Please add a comment for this constructor, and among other things mention if `identity_manager` must not be null."],["ee75f25e_ab928d4b",74,-3,1,"Exposing a non-const object for a function marked as const is an antipattern. Can the latter be removed or const added to the return value? Same below."],["11a9cdc8_ff44a073",73,-2,1,"Nit: please mention that it may be invoked at most once. It would also be nice to call out that destructing `this` will cancel any ongoing request without invoking the callback."],["30b5bd9c_d6dcf9c7",71,-2,1,"Nit: this reads off, how about: *msg.mutable_bag_of_chips() = sync_pb::ChipBag();"],["6d66b733_b621fa59",71,-2,1,"Can you add a comment about why Unretained is safe here? I am assuming that `access_token_fetcher_`'s destruction would cancel any in-flight operations."],["7601ab5d_af18c0cc",75,-2,0,"This triggered a thought... Optional: should the new files be under components/sync/engine? It feels like this could also unblock some code reuse, e.g. when it comes to populating the request proto."],["81969d62_7ec9cc82",71,-2,1,"Optional: I'm a little uneasy that these requests will be hard to distinguish from regular sync traffic (e.g. pollute server-side logs and dashboards). Should be introduce a new origin, or annotate…"],["84ce6cd5_4e5d0a6b",71,-2,1,"Nit: CHECK(callback);"],["8e95c49a_cfa1fdf3",71,-2,1,"Same as before: please add a comment explaning why Unretained is safe."],["c70496b8_80bb8101",71,-2,1,"CHECK(callback_)."],["d7c3fe1e_0529e687",71,-2,1,"Nit: rename to UpdateStateAndNotify or UpdateStateAndRunCallback?"],["efff0b87_34bc77b0",71,-2,0,"There's a lot of code above that would be hard to maintain in the long term and ideally would reuse implementation with the sync engine. Since this is a temporary metric (isn't it), it's probably…"],["f958d697_07d76250",71,-1,1,"Usually metrics get disabled when the metrics setting is off. Is this request only downloading information about signed in accounts? Should we replace the term \"metrics\" with something else? (info,…"]],0,3584],[7268767,20440,83,2.773,2.22,[[30,116]],[["abdb8245_61874930",73,0,1,"Can this move to the Impl class? I always find this pattern odd, that an interface would imply a specific implementation. In fact I would recommend removing this function altogether, because the…"]],0,3585],[7274483,20440,190,5.273,4.339,[[30,0.994,117,1020],[75,0.003,78,2],[74,0.003,6,2]],[],0,3586]]}